# Shell scripts must always check out with LF, even on Windows -- a script
# with CRLF line endings breaks the moment it runs inside a Linux container
# (`sh script.sh` chokes on the trailing \r, e.g. "illegal option -" on a
# perfectly valid `set -eu`). This is the exact bug that silently crash-
# looped the db-backup sidecar: ops/db-backup/backup.sh and restore.sh both
# checked out CRLF and never produced a single successful backup.
*.sh text eol=lf
